<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to March 15.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to March 15.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar </p>
<p>Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June)</p>
<p>sugar crop to March 15 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week March 9-March 15</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,929,768 tns	215,044 tns    11.14 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,826,942 tns	208,710 tns    11.42 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,842,605 tns	206,035 tns    11.18 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to March 15</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    23,871,068 tns    2,554,687 tns    10.70 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    23,097,279 tns    2,435,545 tns    10.54 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    21,934,091 tns    2,287,689 tns    10.43 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 60 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 60 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 59 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
</text>
